From: aston
Subject: [PATCH] runtime: device overlay tool for owner overlays of sealed system files

[payload.runtime] overlay_tool runs a device script on the mounted OS image and adds the directories its report names
to the GPU addon (UniXNU-aston: the InterfaceNamer plugin Info.plist with short wait timeouts).
---
diff --git a/scripts/build-boot-runtime.py b/scripts/build-boot-runtime.py
--- a/scripts/build-boot-runtime.py	2026-11-11 19:45:08.792307500 +0800
+++ b/scripts/build-boot-runtime.py	2026-11-11 19:45:08.792348563 +0800
@@ -274,6 +274,20 @@
                             bundles += [f'audio/{name}', Path(mount) / 'System/Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/HAL' / name]
                         script('addon-add-dir.py', candidate, combined, *bundles)
                         candidate = combined
+                    if request.get('overlay_tool'):
+                        # Owner overlays of sealed system files, made by the device from this OS image: its report names each
+                        # addon prefix and the directory below its output that goes there (the kernel mounts them).
+                        overlay = work / 'overlay'
+                        run(sys.executable, Path(request['device']) / request['overlay_tool'], overlay, '--os-root', mount)
+                        directories = []
+                        for prefix, relative in json.loads((overlay / 'report.json').read_text())['directories'].items():
+                            if (not prefix or Path(prefix).is_absolute() or '..' in Path(prefix).parts or
+                                    Path(relative).is_absolute() or '..' in Path(relative).parts):
+                                raise ValueError('invalid overlay directory')
+                            directories += [prefix, overlay / relative]
+                        combined = work / 'overlay-addon.bin'
+                        script('addon-add-dir.py', candidate, combined, *directories)
+                        candidate = combined
                     addon = out / 'gpuaddon.bin'
                     candidate.replace(addon)
         if addon is None and not want_addon and request.get('boot_shims'):
